# tally 2.3.1, G5's builder (d5; L §8.1): in1 and in2 are one, their days the holes d1 and d2, and their
# amounts differ: the HOLE-SAME question's day prints as its hole prints. Before: a Python repr,
# `Hole([('d1?', 'd1')])`.
=== d5.tally
model d5
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-10
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind twos: event certain
  leg cash: PLN
  leg fee: PLN
place wallet: accounts PLN lives 2025-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input d1: date
input d2: date
input a1: money PLN
input a2: money PLN
input f1: money PLN
move in1: twos
  on d1
  leg cash from world to wallet amount a1
  leg fee from wallet to world amount f1
move in2: twos
  on d2
  leg cash from world to wallet amount a2
  leg fee from wallet to world amount f1
version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  opening[wallet] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  d1 = ?"d1?" "s"
  d2 = ?"d2?" "s"
  a1 = 100.00 PLN "s"
  a2 = 120.00 PLN "s"
  f1 = 1.00 PLN "s"
  same in1 = in2
ask blc: bal(wallet, 2026-03-31)
ask bl4: bal(wallet, 2026-03-04)
ask bl6: bal(wallet, 2026-03-06)
ask amt: sum(m.cash.amount for m in twos over 2026-03)
ask cnt: count(m in twos over 2026-03)
ask c5: count(m in twos over 2026-03-05 .. 2026-03-05)
ask c9: count(m in twos over 2026-03-09 .. 2026-03-09)
ask fl: flows(wallet, 2026-03)
ask fl1: flows(in1.cash, 2026-03)
ask fl2: flows(in2.cash, 2026-03)
ask dys: m.day for m in twos over 2026-03
ask d_1: in1.day
ask d_2: in2.day
ask both: in1.day, in2.day
ask ex: explain bal(wallet, 2026-03-31)
=== expect amt
amt: ?"d1?" (d1) ?"d2?" (d2) ?"in1 and in2 are one, but leg cash differs on ?\"d1?\" (d1): 100.00 PLN (in1) and 120.00 PLN (in2)" (in1, in2)
  cut 2026-06-10
